WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:06.432
I will share with you at least some&nbsp;
kind of historical information.

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:13.152
So in the middle ages in Europe there were these&nbsp;
people called hermits. The most well known type of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:19.152
hermits were ones that lived in secluded places,&nbsp;
like the deep woods, or islands, or mountains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:25.312
or marshes, etc. Being a hermit and living a&nbsp;
life of seclusion, piety, and frugality was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:31.392
seen in medieval christianity as a legitimate path&nbsp;
towards salvation. Hermits were also often seen as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.392 --> 00:00:37.072
wise and many people would try to seek them out&nbsp;
for guidance in religious matters. However, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.072 --> 00:00:42.272
was another very common type of hermit, which&nbsp;
by the time of the 14th century became the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.272 --> 00:00:48.192
common type of hermit, and that is a quote “public&nbsp;
works hermit”. A public works hermit was a hermit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:54.032
that was appointed by either a city or a church&nbsp;
or sometimes even a wealthy individual to patrol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.032 --> 00:01:00.832
and maintain public infrastructure like bridges,&nbsp;
roads, lighthouses, etc. By definition all these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.832 --> 00:01:06.192
things were outside of population centres and,&nbsp;
therefore, hermits seemed like the perfect kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.192 --> 00:01:11.392
of people to maintain them, even if the job of&nbsp;
maintaining them meant that they did come into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.392 --> 00:01:16.112
contact with people sometimes, which kind of&nbsp;
went against the whole idea of being a hermit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.112 --> 00:01:21.072
but there where profits to be made so to many&nbsp;
people it did not matter. To give you an example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:28.752
highway and bridge hermits could exact tolls. The&nbsp;
initial point of these tolls and payments was to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.752 --> 00:01:34.592
cover the costs of maintaining the bridges and&nbsp;
roads, hence the job was still one of none-profit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.592 --> 00:01:40.192
and frugality. However, over time the hermits&nbsp;
and or the people/institutions that appointed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:45.392
them to these positions started to exact higher&nbsp;
payments than was needed for the maintenance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.392 --> 00:01:54.432
and so made a profit which could sometimes be&nbsp;
fairly high. This is probably why the practice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.432 --> 00:02:00.032
of public works hermits became so popular in the&nbsp;
late middle ages over being stuck on a mountain.

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:05.152
So, that’s a quick medieval story about&nbsp;
hermits and their occupations. Anyways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.152 --> 00:02:08.992
high to late medieval guilds video coming&nbsp;
at some point early next year hopefully.

